greg@clove.cs.adelaide.edu.au (Greg Bowering) writes:

>I've tried to run my nethack 3.1.3 in debugging mode (using -D) but
>for some reason it only puts me in discovery mode.
>Any ideas why?

There are two possible reasons, depending on the operating system:
If you play on unix, maybe other multi-user systems, too (I don't know, 
and I've only heard about the unix version), the debugging or wizard
mode is often available only to the user who compiled the game.

On single-user systems, you also have to specify the certain player name
(defined at compile time). On the official 3.1.3 binaries the name is "wizard",
so the commmand line is

nethack -u wizard -D

